From: Fuad Tabba <tabba@google.com>
Date: Tue Jun 23 17:37:01 2026 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: KVM: arm64: Fix free mismatch in alloc_sve_state()

alloc_sve_state() allocates with alloc_pages_exact() but frees with
kfree() on the kvm_share_hyp() error path. kfree() on
alloc_pages_exact() memory is wrong because alloc_pages_exact() calls
split_page() to yield order-0 pages, so kfree() frees only the head
page and leaks the rest. The destroy path in kvm_arm_vcpu_destroy()
already uses free_pages_exact() correctly.

Use free_pages_exact() in the error path to match the allocator.

Fixes: 9251f19da0f66 ("ANDROID: KVM: arm64: Donate the memory for the guest SVE state for protected VMs")
Bug: 458241298
Change-Id: Ic7672178f9913a6e06263106111c5c9b70eb45cc
Signed-off-by: Fuad Tabba <tabba@google.com>

Origin: android.googlesource.com/kernel/common aa4a96722c643dc7f9e114d95e1e1e8056f87670
Batch: B-2 (P4 kvm/pKVM cluster) - Class A, apply as-is; predicted ABI delta zero

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/reset.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/reset.c
index 059b703..6b9a207 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/reset.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/reset.c
@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@ static int alloc_sve_state(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu)
 
 	ret = kvm_share_hyp(buf, buf + reg_sz);
 	if (ret) {
-		kfree(buf);
+		free_pages_exact(buf, reg_sz);
 		return ret;
 	}
 
